#########################################################################
                           SOFTWARE FOUNDATIONS
#########################################################################

This directory contains both Rocq scripts (.v files) and generated HTML
files for Volume 1 of the Software Foundations electronic textbook
series.

  - Preface.v or Preface.html
    The place to start reading, including details on how to install
    required software

  - index.html
    The book's cover page and navigation starting point

  - deps.html
    Overview of the ordering of chapters

  - LICENSE
    Explanation of how these files may be redistributed

Building and checking the homework
----------------------------------
Use Rocq 9.0.0. If installed with opam, activate your switch first:

    eval "$(opam env)"
    make Lists.vo ListsTest.vo Poly.vo PolyTest.vo Tactics.vo TacticsTest.vo

The build compiles the required earlier chapters automatically. For just
one chapter, use e.g. `make Tactics.vo TacticsTest.vo`.
Unfinished exercises remain Admitted; a successful build does not mean
that all exercises are complete. Read the test output for remaining axioms.

Working in VS Code on macOS
--------------------------
Open this entire folder in VS Code, so VsRocq reads `_CoqProject` and its
`-Q . LF` library mapping. Use the VsRocq extension with a matching
vsrocq-language-server installed in your opam switch. Set `vsrocq.path`
in your user settings to the output of `opam var bin` plus `/vsrocqtop`.

With a .v file active, Cmd+Shift+B builds that chapter and its dependencies.
The "Rocq: check current homework" task also runs the Lists, Poly, and
Tactics test files. Both tasks use `opam exec` to select the switch's tools.

Makefile.coq, Makefile.coq.conf, and .Makefile.coq.d are generated locally
and ignored by Git because they contain paths specific to each machine.
When moving an existing checkout to another machine, run `make clean`
before building to discard its old generated files.
